# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots vsftpd with the vulnerable config (ssl_enable=NO) and
# then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the daemon is ALREADY RUNNING when the agent starts, which is what makes
#     the "fixed the config but never restarted the service" case detectable;
#   * PID 1 is still `sleep infinity`, so restarting vsftpd cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must RESTART the service, not merely start it
# if absent - the service is already up with the vulnerable configuration.
